The '''Castejón Metro Ferreyra Line''' ({{Lang-bl|Linia de Metro de Castejón a Ferreyra}}) is a [[W:Rapid transit|subway]] line in [[Castejón]], [[Balisca]], operated by the [[Castejón Metro]]. The line runs between [[Madrilena Station|Madrilena]] in [[Calañas]] in the west and [[Cipreses]] ([[Limón]]) in the east. The official name is '''Line No. 12 Ferreyra Line'''.

The line is named after [[Ferreyra]] ({{Literal translation|blacksmith}}), a [[Planned communities in Balisca|new town]] and [[W:Interchange station|interchange station]] that it passes through. On maps and signboards, the line is shown in brown. Stations carry the letter "F" followed by a two-digit number. 

